From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Blumenkrantz <michael.blumenkrantz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 13:15:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan/wsi: don't let x11 swapchain threads inherit a pinned
 affinity

with mesa_pin_threads the app thread is pinned to one cpu before the
swapchain exists, and the x11 present and event threads inherited that cpu
and preempted the app thread on every present

Generated-by: LLM
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45386>
(cherry picked from commit 0204fb3d9fb105f99ffdfdcf18cceaad9f0de117)
---
 src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c
index 532e9a2067a..003ef7a79aa 100644
--- a/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c
+++ b/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_x11.c
@@ -2342,6 +2342,7 @@ x11_manage_event_queue(void *state)
 {
    struct x11_swapchain *chain = state;
    u_thread_setname("WSI swapchain event");
+   util_set_current_thread_full_affinity();
 
    /* While there is an outstanding IDLE we should wait for it.
     * In FLIP modes at most one image will not be driver owned eventually.
@@ -2562,6 +2563,8 @@ x11_manage_present_queue(void *state)
          wsi_x11_get_connection((struct wsi_device*)chain->base.wsi, chain->conn);
    VkResult result = VK_SUCCESS;
 
+   util_set_current_thread_full_affinity();
+
    u_thread_setname("WSI swapchain queue");
 
    uint64_t target_msc = 0;
-- 
